# A Tern node's own fix and its satellite receiver (companion version 8), and turning the node off
# (version 9).
#
# Position is where the node takes itself to be - its receiver's fix or the last a client gave it -
# read here rather than typed, then the receiver as a switch and whose fix it is under it. Off, the
# last fix stays the node's. The Radio card's details end on Shutdown, the row Meshtastic's
# shutdown uses, behind the same confirm; for a Tern node the press sends OFF.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 300
config
receiver fixed 9
protocol tern 9
tab settings
hold 800
# Position is the second of the four sections a Tern node has.
key down 1
key a
hold 1600
key down 2
key right
hold 1600
key b
key b
tab radio
hold 900
# The Radio card's details, and down to Power.
key down 9
key up
key a
hold 1200
key down 40
key up
hold 1600
key a
hold 2400
